#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124247 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "526b792b-9952-5dae-bcd6-15564c0e013f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3131" :question/problem "Find $\\nabla f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,\\pi)$ given that $f(x,y) = (x - y)\\cos y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-(x-y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\text{ }i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(x-y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the gradient at the specified point, we substitute $(x,y)= (1,\\pi)$ into the above, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(1,\\pi ) & ={f}_{x}(1,\\pi )\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(1,\\pi )\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\text{ }i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +(1-\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124248 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2c7ce2-f053-57af-9f4d-54bd3a41648a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Three Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "bfade25e-065a-5c66-a554-9ee4e9559a55" :question/math-academy-id "e-3132" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\nabla g(x,y,z)$   at $(2,-1,3)$ if $g(x,y,z) = x^2 + xyz.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xyz) \\\\  & =2x+yz \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xyz) \\\\  & =0+xz \\\\  & =xz \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+xyz) \\\\  & =0+xy \\\\  & =xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x+yz)\\text{ }i+(xz)\\text{ }j+(xy)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇g(2,-1,3) & =(2(2)+(-1)(3))\\text{ }i+2(3)\\text{ }j+2(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =1\\text{ }i+6\\text{ }j-2\\text{ }k \\\\  & =i+6\\text{ }j-2\\text{ }k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124249 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/id #uuid "b2549d7b-07c2-5f2f-89a3-2cccecf2ba22" :question/math-academy-id "e-3133" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)= (y-4)\\ln (x-2),$ find the points $(x, y)$ where $\\nabla f(x,y) = \\mathbf 0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((y-4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{y-4}{x-2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((y-4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x,y) = \\dfrac {y-4}{x-2} \\, \\mathbf i + \\ln(x-2) \\, \\mathbf j.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve $\\nabla f(x,y) = \\mathbf 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {y-4}{x-2} \\, \\mathbf i + \\ln(x-2) \\, \\mathbf j = 0 \\  \\mathbf i + 0\\ \\mathbf j\n$$\n\nBy equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf{i}$ on both sides of the equation (and similarly with $\\mathbf{j}$), we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y-4}{x-2} &=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2) &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y-4=0,$ which means $y=4.$  From the second equation, we obtain $\\ln(x-2)=0,$ which means that $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, $\\nabla f(x,y) =\\mathbf  0$ at the point $(3,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124251 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67cfec73-130c-5b68-a2e0-5f12837bfc81" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Using the Properties of the Gradient"}] :question/id #uuid "67e9bcb5-4bf2-56b8-8d82-95355841eaaa" :question/math-academy-id "e-3150" :question/problem "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y) g(x,y)$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =xy,\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ g(x,y) & =\\sqrt{xy},\\, &  & ∇g(x,y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2y}\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $g(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\nabla [fg] = g \\, \\nabla\\! f  + f \\, \\nabla\\! g.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule shown above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)g(x,y)] & =g(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇g(x,y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{xy}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j)+xy(\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{xy}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j)+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{xy}}{2}(y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191fd92c-d897-524f-85fa-cdc13fdab7ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,i+\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{xy}{e}^{x/y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573447} {:answer/id #uuid "23f78021-8f94-5150-a450-38155414595c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}y}{e}^{x/y}\\,i+\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{x{y}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573469} {:answer/id #uuid "371110b6-46e3-596b-9575-499451fd3d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-y}{{x}^{2}y}{e}^{x/y}\\,i+\\frac{x-1}{x{y}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573495} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd76aaa-4503-5af9-b4d2-4e88ce7a5557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573628} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ca5fae-3d83-517f-b574-e5688492df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-y}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,i+\\frac{y-x}{xy}{e}^{x/y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5ca5fae-3d83-517f-b574-e5688492df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-y}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\,i+\\frac{y-x}{xy}{e}^{x/y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573638} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9ee866-f5ad-511c-b339-3c9eaf2191fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11d17df4-8621-5dfb-b614-0130a53b1042" :question/math-academy-id "q-127649" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}{e}^{x/y},$ find $∇f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{y}{x}{e}^{x/y}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}){e}^{x/y} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-y}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{x/y} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y}{x}{e}^{x/y}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}){e}^{x/y} \\\\  & =\\frac{y-x}{xy}{e}^{x/y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\frac{x-y}{{x}^{2}}{e}^{x/y}\\text{ }i+\\frac{y-x}{xy}{e}^{x/y}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2c7ce2-f053-57af-9f4d-54bd3a41648a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Three Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "514f6510-65a6-5c71-8eca-34568a35dcba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y{x}^{y-1}\\,i+({x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+z{y}^{z-1})j+{y}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383092} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1164dc-4f74-5f63-8956-517c46e081b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y{x}^{y-1}\\,i+z{y}^{z-1}\\,j+{y}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383093} {:answer/id #uuid "37e9d54a-963a-50c9-af62-5869773b3bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,i+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,j+({x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+z{y}^{z-1})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383094} {:answer/id #uuid "daceaefe-76b2-57db-9142-cb9036ed18b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+z{y}^{z-1})i+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+{y}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383095} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a91458-30b5-5353-b216-4f46dc771583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y{x}^{y-1}\\,i+z{y}^{z-1}\\,j+z{y}^{z-1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "514f6510-65a6-5c71-8eca-34568a35dcba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y{x}^{y-1}\\,i+({x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+z{y}^{z-1})j+{y}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383092} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa7309b8-5993-5bb2-9ecd-ce38b1c0b74d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf052c6a-faee-5b8c-b178-4c397426507c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127945" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{y}+{y}^{z},$ find $∇f(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{y}+{y}^{z}) \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{y}+{y}^{z}) \\\\  & ={x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+z{y}^{z-1} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{y}+{y}^{z}) \\\\  & ={y}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1}\\,i+({x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+z{y}^{z-1})j+{y}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2c7ce2-f053-57af-9f4d-54bd3a41648a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Three Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096a33d6-d118-5767-9aef-e8a314eac3cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{1/2}}(x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573435} {:answer/id #uuid "3070acd5-da6e-5912-9c2f-3fa61b9ecd1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}({x}^{2}\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573486} {:answer/id #uuid "bb0eed41-4001-5d69-afa8-86d50d932215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{1/2}}({x}^{2}\\,i+{y}^{2}\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573665} {:answer/id #uuid "df98d7d6-f700-5365-a939-7b86231547af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}(x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573717} {:answer/id #uuid "fe18764d-76e8-51ba-bcfd-15ecbbf56867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}(x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df98d7d6-f700-5365-a939-7b86231547af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}(x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573717} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccf85ad2-68ea-542a-9e96-be9081261312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d01726f-52af-5592-8eb9-d6abaee05cc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127950" :question/problem "Find $∇f(x,y,z),$  given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{1/2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{z}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(-\\frac{x}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}})i+(-\\frac{y}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}})j+(-\\frac{z}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3/2}}(x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fe7a32f-bd64-5c3a-ac51-aa8e847ab23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439495} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b19982-26ea-52cf-bfb6-891798ebe687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fe7a32f-bd64-5c3a-ac51-aa8e847ab23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9b26fe-a648-553a-a416-e7a5675ab1fe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8879c732-ca2d-5143-a4fe-4257993d10ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439497} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d1f38f-73c6-5480-a2d4-f3c457b36e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d1f38f-73c6-5480-a2d4-f3c457b36e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439498} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ac6491-2fe7-5147-88bb-c17f0c42377d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9a47546-8467-57ce-8aa2-a8af7a03a45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439499} {:answer/id #uuid "9a881647-dacf-5b22-a11c-6dbd54eab45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a881647-dacf-5b22-a11c-6dbd54eab45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439500} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5b81800-b1bd-502a-8929-18d2b7af4a18" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c3587a5-2b35-5b4d-8516-1a3e694d12a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439501} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a10786-54a3-53dd-acf2-86b3f03692c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c3587a5-2b35-5b4d-8516-1a3e694d12a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439501} :answer-field/id #uuid "0962b3c3-8729-55fc-a737-e4fe61f7b385" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48261b12-c86c-55b1-9e2a-f38acbfa450a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128517" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,$ find the points $(x,y),$ for $0\\le y<\\pi ,$ where $∇f(x,y)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,0)$\n- **II.** $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$\n- **III.** $(1,0)$\n- **IV.** $(1,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y)=2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,i+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y)=0:$ \n\n$$\n2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,i+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0 \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=0\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y=0,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.$\n\n- For $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\nTherefore, $∇f(x,y)=0,$ for $0\\le y<\\pi ,$ at two points: $(1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e2cbf2-c37b-543b-b26a-9f17ca2646c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573471} {:answer/id #uuid "2f242f1f-5816-58b4-87d2-bb76e329eb25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573482} {:answer/id #uuid "34a34f22-0899-537a-88cc-dd3d3b4a724a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573491} {:answer/id #uuid "6e3a39c1-6a68-5668-b506-a7865d804a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ and $(0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573558} {:answer/id #uuid "e9726b7e-5741-549b-8af7-327964dd414c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e3a39c1-6a68-5668-b506-a7865d804a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ and $(0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573558} :answer-field/id #uuid "73231a02-8c67-5ffc-9fab-d156f24315bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e83d5b90-8fee-5f1e-85b9-d81d6b0e4f2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128518" :question/problem "Given that $h(x,y)=({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}){e}^{x}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇h(x,y)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}){e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x{e}^{x}+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}){e}^{x} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2x-{y}^{2}){e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}){e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-2y{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y)=({x}^{2}+2x-{y}^{2}){e}^{x}\\,i-2y{e}^{x}\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇h(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+2x-{y}^{2}){e}^{x}\\,i-2y{e}^{x}\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+2x-{y}^{2}){e}^{x} &=0, \\\\ -2y{e}^{x} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+2x-{0}^{2}){e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ x(x+2){e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $∇h(x,y)=0$ at two points: $(-2,0)$ and $(0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67cfec73-130c-5b68-a2e0-5f12837bfc81" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Using the Properties of the Gradient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "529ed7e8-aeeb-52a8-a2e3-bef0a5d5a876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))({x}^{2}\\text{ }i+{y}^{2}\\text{ }j+{z}^{2}\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573525} {:answer/id #uuid "6f70fa62-73aa-5b1f-a8b5-d6e2bc56dbbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))(i+j+k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573561} {:answer/id #uuid "6fad20ac-6c37-508b-8c26-3e7dcbdd2f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))(yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573563} {:answer/id #uuid "7629053b-c6ce-5444-9d41-37da2cce7540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))((y+z)\\text{ }i+(x+z)\\text{ }j+(x+y)\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573578} {:answer/id #uuid "f331fb10-4f55-506a-a338-4ed215d3e807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))(x\\text{ }i+y\\text{ }j+z\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fad20ac-6c37-508b-8c26-3e7dcbdd2f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))(yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573563} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb97214-9396-5a5e-8c44-9c78f53576a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7f1d01a7-3767-50a6-8161-9fa62992d18d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128524" :question/problem "What is the gradient of the product $f(x,y,z)h(x,y,z)$ if $f(x,y,z)=xyz$ and $h(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=f∇h+h∇f.\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)=yz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)=xz \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz)=xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\text{ }k=yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the partial derivatives of $h(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))=\\frac{1}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂h}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂h}{∂y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂h}{∂z}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y,z)h(x,y,z)] & =f(x,y,z)∇h(x,y,z)+h(x,y,z)∇f(x,y,z) \\\\  & =xyz(\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)(yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =\\frac{xyz}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{xyz}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{xyz}{z}\\text{ }k+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)(yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)(yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k) \\\\  & =(1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))(yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67cfec73-130c-5b68-a2e0-5f12837bfc81" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Using the Properties of the Gradient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e191e44-d94c-5870-b0c8-ced1667641d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}((x-y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(y-x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573456} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab883f7-d2c5-5df8-91ea-93715df943d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}((y+x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})-x)j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573554} {:answer/id #uuid "8f2d08a1-9016-5fb7-8c20-20d22247482a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}((x-y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(y-x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573607} {:answer/id #uuid "cd63465f-5f06-58e0-beae-c3c0a61fc922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}((y-x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(x+y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573695} {:answer/id #uuid "d1205bef-1a93-51b6-9180-985157270273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}((y-x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(x+y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ab883f7-d2c5-5df8-91ea-93715df943d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}((y+x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})-x)j)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573554} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f99c31-3839-5c38-b360-b7a08fb69629" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce288280-35f0-55c7-872a-791cfea323e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-128528" :question/problem "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y)h(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}),\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j, &  &  \\\\ h(x,y) & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\, &  & ∇h(x,y)=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=h∇f+f∇h.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)h(x,y)] & =h(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇h(x,y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j)+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j+\\frac{x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{y+x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})-x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}((y+x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}))i+(y\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})-x)j).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a668efeb-9196-55f8-9b55-0356db924def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (5)/((x - y)^{2})(yi - xj)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122241} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fd1360-8206-5747-923f-e6bf5289202a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (5)/((x - y)^{2})(xi - yj)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122242} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c956e9-6137-5353-ae04-fcff7a793ac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5)/((x - y)^{2})(yi + xj)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122243} {:answer/id #uuid "647b8faa-7bab-5d6a-a230-2a682d9c494b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5(xi - yj)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122244} {:answer/id #uuid "6d99f357-3be3-5bf2-92f7-0e5cb85c4117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5(yi - xj)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122245}] :answer-field/id #uuid "62bc8146-116e-5fde-8c73-4e57f913d974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9824799-8fb2-5e3e-9b52-a3b623c77e1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-35988" :question/problem "Given $f(x, y) = \\frac{3x + 2y}{x - y}$, find $∇f(x, y)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2c7ce2-f053-57af-9f4d-54bd3a41648a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Three Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94b23f6d-fcbc-5f05-bdfa-551e5a601813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2xz}\\text{ }(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)i+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385333} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb1b5c1-0c20-551c-a0c4-1c105471790f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2xz}\\text{ }(zi+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+x\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385334} {:answer/id #uuid "0886912b-e3e5-5d97-a4f7-8d67907aca83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)i+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385335} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f5b6bf-05e5-54bc-b294-aa5357db39ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }(zi+y\\text{ }j+x\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385336} {:answer/id #uuid "24c26190-fbac-5847-9741-c5fdf4a37862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2xz}\\text{ }(zi+y\\text{ }j+x\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b23f6d-fcbc-5f05-bdfa-551e5a601813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2xz}\\text{ }(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)i+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }k)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385333} :answer-field/id #uuid "63bf46dd-0351-5c7b-a783-d87b1b22bab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f2c8781-0baa-5cdd-8cbc-03cc6b1166f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-35989" :question/problem "Given  $g(x,y,z)={e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)$, find $∇g(x,y,z).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)) \\\\  & =2z{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1) \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)) \\\\  & =2y{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1) \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)) \\\\  & =2x{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2z{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }i+2y{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2x{e}^{2xz}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2xz}\\text{ }(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)i+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}-1)\\text{ }k)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3571c649-0531-50fb-81be-aa0dc6824b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\pi ,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321556} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff57b68-3c51-53bb-b23d-d256805ec32e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321773} {:answer/id #uuid "a280209e-a266-5259-8e3c-561a3617e91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\pi ,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322429} {:answer/id #uuid "dec9e1b5-c792-5421-b9a9-29ad4b32bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322888} {:answer/id #uuid "f61c2261-0bcc-57ad-8951-891f80c64105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dec9e1b5-c792-5421-b9a9-29ad4b32bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322888} :answer-field/id #uuid "81886d51-1e5e-5e76-8e7d-103ef37f4bdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ae928cb-8fc1-5d80-9fc4-2442ff5c0221" :question/math-academy-id "q-36005" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇h(x,y)$ at $(1,1)$ if $h(x,y)=4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇h(x,y) & =⟨{h}_{x}(x,y),\\,{h}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y,\\,\\frac{4x}{{y}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ ∇h(1,1) & =⟨4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1,\\,\\frac{4\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi ,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a66e67-c420-5bae-9224-c8f5d4fde075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321440} {:answer/id #uuid "47baee24-d042-549a-8151-b2da72dc39a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321711} {:answer/id #uuid "9abaf78d-69a4-535f-a08b-0a3417313ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322375} {:answer/id #uuid "c8af8076-8ba0-5745-9225-6f71fe87a617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨16,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322707} {:answer/id #uuid "cc23bd77-b2ea-5ecd-832e-27ef06e5c5fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc23bd77-b2ea-5ecd-832e-27ef06e5c5fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322734} :answer-field/id #uuid "561a4834-955d-5829-ab93-034d86fd0c74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b4ba176-5939-5525-9fa4-02ef800efbcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-36909" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇f(x,y)$ at $(2,1)$ if $f(x,y)={x}^{2}\\sqrt{y+3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y+3}) \\\\  & =2x\\sqrt{y+3} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}\\sqrt{y+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y+3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨{f}_{x}(x,y),\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2x\\sqrt{y+3},\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y+3}}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =⟨2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{1+3},\\,\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{1+3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2c7ce2-f053-57af-9f4d-54bd3a41648a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Three Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e393b4-8a81-5128-9ba6-326770dd3c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321197} {:answer/id #uuid "46cf9748-7a8c-51e8-a98f-bf480e7d4abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{yz}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{yz}\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321705} {:answer/id #uuid "5277d147-5423-52ea-9448-c91d7f890aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321796} {:answer/id #uuid "76d89040-9cda-5314-8747-132b54e35625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2yz}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2yz}\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322073} {:answer/id #uuid "fa45680f-55c0-5cbc-847f-d3b13a4ac29e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05e393b4-8a81-5128-9ba6-326770dd3c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321197} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bd27916-0e07-570f-8b09-3b81d2a1b865" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e287a6b3-141e-5735-ae69-360760a9ed55" :question/math-academy-id "q-36968" :question/problem "Find $∇g(x,y,z)$ given that  $g(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz})) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2y} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{x+2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{yz})) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{yz}}\\cdot y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+2}}i+\\frac{1}{2y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{2z}\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124443 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3991a54-342b-5cd0-87e2-606146240555" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Two Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13f2352f-c772-5b68-86ce-95f7bacd28ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-2},\\,1-2{e}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573444} {:answer/id #uuid "2307c7b2-134e-5025-8a74-fbb98b146890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+{e}^{-2},\\,2{e}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573467} {:answer/id #uuid "48360c0b-9b76-50a5-b9fe-64c831454fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+{e}^{2},\\,-1-2{e}^{-2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573512} {:answer/id #uuid "d5654a3d-6031-5f77-bd64-23ea9fdafc83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+{e}^{-2},\\,-1-2{e}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573707} {:answer/id #uuid "f4aa270d-e9bc-54d9-8748-1cd6abbd596d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+{e}^{2},\\,1+2{e}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5654a3d-6031-5f77-bd64-23ea9fdafc83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+{e}^{-2},\\,-1-2{e}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573707} :answer-field/id #uuid "7de27bb1-b0f3-5c6b-a656-0106b44d5e3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b4c3f21-cba5-5b1e-bb44-0204d0b1fcfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-37341" :question/problem "Evaluate the gradient of $g(x,y)$ at the point $({e}^{2},1)$ if $g(x,y)=(x+y)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+y)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2})+(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}+1+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x+y)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2})+(x+y)\\cdot (-2y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}-2xy-2{y}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3{y}^{2}-2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the gradient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨{g}_{x}(x,y),\\,{g}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{y}^{2}+1+\\frac{y}{x},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3{y}^{2}-2xy⟩ \\\\ ∇g({e}^{2},1) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-{1}^{2}+1+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-3\\cdot {1}^{2}-2\\cdot {e}^{2}\\cdot 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2+{e}^{-2},-1-2{e}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67cfec73-130c-5b68-a2e0-5f12837bfc81" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Using the Properties of the Gradient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "576000fb-2c90-5558-b5c8-6c3356424f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x+y)}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+{({x}^{2}+y)}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573534} {:answer/id #uuid "aa75d4dc-66ca-5155-af31-d75936f122fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2{x}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+(x+2{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573646} {:answer/id #uuid "aeeee72c-3251-5d24-ba38-ce48802c8cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+{y}^{2}{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573650} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e125e5-0ea1-5031-b8ac-f4d68b529132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+2x){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573706} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ef9603-2213-5da9-8ecc-2e5e696a90e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0ef9603-2213-5da9-8ecc-2e5e696a90e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573718} :answer-field/id #uuid "a21aceed-9468-56fb-b467-8df32c0f6017" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "807b4074-7dcc-59b6-a5c1-37bc5db08161" :question/math-academy-id "q-65135" :question/problem "What is the gradient of the product $f(x,y)g(x,y)$ if $f(x,y)={e}^{x+y}$ and $g(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $g(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fg]=f\\,∇\\,g+g\\,∇\\,f\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the first order partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+y})={e}^{x+y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+y})={e}^{x+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\text{ }j={e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the partial derivatives of $g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =\\frac{∂g}{∂x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\text{ }j=2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)g(x,y)] & =({e}^{x+y})(2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j)+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})({e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =2x{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+2y{e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y+{y}^{2}){e}^{x+y}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124444 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2c7ce2-f053-57af-9f4d-54bd3a41648a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient of a Function of Three Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a21b9f7-4aaa-5471-bf82-f2d8ab4a05d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336422} {:answer/id #uuid "71cc0d72-27c7-5788-8341-714d4d503875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2y+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337049} {:answer/id #uuid "78722099-cc9a-5084-9630-ca6c5d2d30e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337116} {:answer/id #uuid "7a839402-601f-5953-874b-788c1ff02eff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz-1})\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz-1})\\text{ }j+({x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz-1})\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337136} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9d6b72-745e-56b9-86ea-4dab4db1e685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+x{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+y{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+z{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78722099-cc9a-5084-9630-ca6c5d2d30e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337116} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0b11fb-76fe-57a4-9209-9720c0dc1087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d8f2390-7ede-5da9-be05-731bb79d1f06" :question/math-academy-id "q-71425" :question/problem "Find $∇g(x,y,z)$ given that  $g(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+{e}^{xyz}) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  the gradient is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\text{ }i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+yz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}y{z}^{2}+xz{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }j+(2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}z+xy{e}^{xyz})\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f709b8d-e22d-555e-8f82-4b819b741a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385538} {:answer/id #uuid "4f628e18-1e56-5031-998e-e94575d669fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385539} {:answer/id #uuid "8a817cfe-6e50-5534-9c89-401a91beed6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385540} {:answer/id #uuid "6f89f99e-c222-5f75-b88f-1f3ed3be632f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385541} {:answer/id #uuid "55d2d586-a13f-55b7-99b9-71d0fd4b3d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f709b8d-e22d-555e-8f82-4b819b741a2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385538} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5955cf1-cc26-55ec-8c2a-34ff0cdd5429" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "191461eb-d37c-55af-a5cc-b1cdcbe5989a" :question/math-academy-id "q-71437" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=4xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇g(x,y)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4y+0-2x \\\\  & =2(2y-x) \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4x+2y-0 \\\\  & =2(2x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y)=2(2y-x)\\,i+2(2x+y)\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n2(2y-x)\\,i+2(2x+y)\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y-x &=0 \\\\ 2x+y &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=2y.$ Substituting these into the second equation, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2y)+y & =0 \\\\ 5y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get $x=2\\cdot 0=0.$\n\nTherefore, $∇g(x,y)=0$ at the point $(0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b0c95e4-c6e9-54b6-a15d-ea7087127b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439909} {:answer/id #uuid "a2e5d812-4735-5fc8-b852-eeaeeaafc9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c95e4-c6e9-54b6-a15d-ea7087127b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439909} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d2c8b7-ca4d-57e5-9519-e48520596596" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8aaf15a-211e-5baf-b019-f56f2c0415e5" :answer/type 