r/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439915} :answer-field/id #uuid "47cda995-fd9f-589a-85d9-cfbd97013861" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440315} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "405c5964-ed58-56db-a7d0-221666926760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439917} {:answer/id #uuid "7990ef8e-46b5-5559-a2c5-aa8d65421d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "405c5964-ed58-56db-a7d0-221666926760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439917} :answer-field/id #uuid "84892d33-55b9-54ef-a343-3de68b52e47d" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d182b83a-f3d7-59a8-a2df-a282497de34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439919} {:answer/id #uuid "767b3c80-fc75-58d7-a96d-c20b801d7033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d182b83a-f3d7-59a8-a2df-a282497de34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439919} :answer-field/id #uuid "71df9b88-565a-50cb-b76e-a7999233dce6" :answer-field/key "VI" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c503ae86-f71f-5a21-9c90-e19ce4d410a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-71474" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇f(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,-1,-1)$\n- **II.** $(-1,-1,1)$\n- **III.** $(-1,1,-1)$\n- **IV.** $(-1,1,1)$\n- **V.** $(1,-1,-1)$\n- **VI.** $(1,1,1)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}+0-\\frac{1}{z{x}^{2}}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}+0-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{zx}-z) \\\\  & =0+0-\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}x}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}\\,i-\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}\\,j-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}-\\frac{z+y}{{x}^{2}yz}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+x}{x{y}^{2}}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x}=0\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x=-1.$ Substituting these into the third equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1+{z}^{2}x}{{z}^{2}x} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1+{z}^{2}(-1)}{{z}^{2}(-1)} & =0 \\\\ 1-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{z+y}{(-1)^{2}yz} & =0 \\\\ z+y & =0 \\\\ y & =-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $z=1,$ we have $y=-1$ and when $z=-1,$ we have $y=1.$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(-1,-1,1)$ and $(-1,1,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00852e0a-f6f6-5c5a-ac0e-5aab7917034a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385545} {:answer/id #uuid "0a138de7-1cdb-5fca-ab9b-192f03014909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(e,e,e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385546} {:answer/id #uuid "4db23065-4328-5f87-98fa-c2f53e71285d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{e},\\frac{1}{e},\\frac{1}{e})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385547} {:answer/id #uuid "c45fae02-a3c6-5e5b-83c3-515185ddf33b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385548} {:answer/id #uuid "965bb97e-ab1f-5bcd-b8b9-68650da44bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "965bb97e-ab1f-5bcd-b8b9-68650da44bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385549} :answer-field/id #uuid "12e34691-896f-5bb6-afac-57e259bb49f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ceb4f40b-ddfe-5165-8e9a-092d10842d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-71475" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z$, find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇g(x,y,z)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+0+0-1-0-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z) \\\\  & =0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}+0-0-1-0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+z\\operatorname{ln}⁡z-x-y-z) \\\\  & =0+0+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+z\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}-0-0-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z+1-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,k.$ \n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficient of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x &=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y &=0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=1.$  Similarly, from the second and third equations, we obtain $y=1$ and $z=1.$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y,z)=0$ at the point $(1,1,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67cfec73-130c-5b68-a2e0-5f12837bfc81" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Using the Properties of the Gradient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23400f54-8b3f-5ebc-b598-c7818f4586c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336361} {:answer/id #uuid "34196f13-9af3-5e84-930f-7cdc02f6b4ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\text{ }i+y\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336521} {:answer/id #uuid "78b044f0-5569-5fa2-b926-c4fa16e63d1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337118} {:answer/id #uuid "86424757-d1c0-5142-865b-bc737655d636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337246} {:answer/id #uuid "8a45146a-092c-5746-a1f7-52f22a8062eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78b044f0-5569-5fa2-b926-c4fa16e63d1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337118} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa16c79-d297-52a5-b07c-cccb5e15aa03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91443473-cbb1-5ab2-b98b-379cda895777" :question/math-academy-id "q-71476" :question/problem "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y)h(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2},\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=(2xy+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2xy)\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ h(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{xy},\\, &  & ∇h(x,y)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $h(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fh]=h\\,∇\\,f+f\\,∇\\,h\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)h(x,y)] & =h(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇h(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xy}((2xy+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2xy)\\text{ }j)+({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{x{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2xy+{y}^{2}}{xy}\\text{ }i+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy}{xy}\\text{ }j)+(-\\frac{{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}y}\\text{ }i-\\frac{{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2x+y}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{x+2y}{y}\\text{ }j)+(-\\frac{x+y}{x}\\text{ }i-\\frac{x+y}{y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{x+y}{x}+\\frac{2x+y}{x})\\text{ }i+(-\\frac{x+y}{y}+\\frac{x+2y}{y})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124447 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67cfec73-130c-5b68-a2e0-5f12837bfc81" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Using the Properties of the Gradient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2294583c-d437-5eae-b90b-2cda9099190e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\text{ }i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573464} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec5a200-fd15-5ef2-88d6-afbc29d7c528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573630} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ae61c4-5858-560b-8562-9483edee1e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573659} {:answer/id #uuid "f66dcd21-76d7-5ee3-8517-4944100e0abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-1)\\text{ }i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-1)\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573757} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6af3d1-58f8-58d1-98b6-c239cd2565eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\text{ }i+(x+y)\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ec5a200-fd15-5ef2-88d6-afbc29d7c528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573630} :answer-field/id #uuid "128efc33-07e1-500d-bdf0-345d1c5e017b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7be3188-95a1-5bd7-a100-6bc1c7138029" :question/math-academy-id "q-71477" :question/problem "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y)g(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =x+y,\\, &  & ∇f(x,y)=\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j, &  &  \\\\ g(x,y) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y),\\, &  & ∇g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+y}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{x+y}\\text{ }j. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the product of two functions $f(x,y)$ and $g(x,y)$ is given by:\n\n$$\n∇[fg]=g\\,∇\\,f+f\\,∇\\,g\n$$\n\nSo, using this product rule we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇[f(x,y)g(x,y)] & =g(x,y)∇f(x,y)+f(x,y)∇g(x,y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)(\\text{ }i+\\text{ }j)+(x+y)(\\frac{1}{x+y}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{x+y}\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\text{ }i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\text{ }j+\\frac{x+y}{x+y}\\text{ }i+\\frac{x+y}{x+y}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\text{ }i+\\text{ }i)+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\text{ }j+1\\text{ }j) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
